import ../../../testing/driver.dl

document mask test:
    paragraph "Mask" using no UI appearance

set instance to an instance of mask test
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 300 by 200 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view the address of view
set frame to @intrinsic("construct", UI frame, the address of view, true)
set texture to @intrinsic("construct", UI texture, 7 as a pointer, 100, 100)
draw UI texture texture across (UI box at 20 30 sized 100 100) sampling (UI box at 1 0 sized -1 1) masked by (UI box at 50 60 sized 20 10) opaque through 0.8 with opacity 128 on frame
require condition (view's vertex count > 0) reporting "A visible ellipse mask produced no geometry"
set faded and opaque to false
set index to 0
loop while index < view's vertex count:
    set vertex to the item at index in (view's vertices)
    require condition (((vertex's x >= 50.0) and (vertex's x <= 70.0)) and ((vertex's y >= 60.0) and (vertex's y <= 70.0))) reporting "A detail mask painted outside its ellipse bounds"
    require condition ((the absolute value of (vertex's u - (1.0 - (vertex's x - 20.0) / 100.0))) < 0.00001) reporting "A flipped mask lost the full-image texture coordinates"
    if vertex's alpha = 0.0:
        set faded to true
    if vertex's alpha > 0.5:
        set opaque to true
    increment index
require condition (faded and opaque) reporting "A masked image lost its transparent feather or opaque center"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Ellipse masks retain image coordinates, mirrored sampling, opacity and a transparent feather."
